### Try these requests with the VS Code "REST Client" extension while `cds watch` is running
@server = http://localhost:4004

### Browse books (author.name is resolved with $lookup)
GET {{server}}/browse/Books?$select=ID,title,author,price&$orderby=price desc&$top=3

### Filter, search and count
GET {{server}}/browse/Books?$filter=stock gt 100 and contains(title,'e')&$count=true

### Localized texts (German)
GET {{server}}/browse/Books(201)?$select=title,descr
Accept-Language: de

### Order a book (reduces stock)
POST {{server}}/browse/submitOrder
Authorization: Basic bob:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book": 201, "quantity": 2 }

### Expand authors with their books
GET {{server}}/admin/Authors?$expand=books($select=title,stock;$orderby=title)
Authorization: Basic alice:

### Analytics: OData $apply - stock per author
GET {{server}}/analytics/Books?$apply=groupby((author_ID),aggregate(stock with sum as totalStock))&$orderby=totalStock desc
Authorization: Basic alice:

### Analytics: OData $apply - filter, aggregate, top
GET {{server}}/analytics/Books?$apply=filter(price gt 12)/groupby((currency_code),aggregate(price with average as avgPrice,$count as books))/orderby(books desc)/top(2)
Authorization: Basic alice:

### Analytics: custom function with CQL groupBy over a path
GET {{server}}/analytics/stockByGenre()
Authorization: Basic alice:

### Analytics: having, orderBy, top/skip
GET {{server}}/analytics/topAuthors(minBooks=1,top=2,skip=0)
Authorization: Basic alice:

### Create a draft (Fiori) ...
POST {{server}}/admin/Books
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ID": 999, "title": "My first MongoDB book", "author_ID": 101, "stock": 10, "price": "9.99" }

### ... and activate it
POST {{server}}/admin/Books(ID=999,IsActiveEntity=false)/AdminService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Analytics app: total sales per region (donut)
GET {{server}}/analytics/salesByRegion()

### Analytics app: total stock per book (bar)
GET {{server}}/analytics/stockByBook()

### Analytics app: total sales per day (line)
GET {{server}}/analytics/salesByDay()

### Analytics app: revenue and units sold per book (column + line)
GET {{server}}/analytics/salesByBook()
